The slag layer thickness,  δ ox , was measured at the surface and the sides separately, as both can be different. For that purpose,  δ ox  was calculated based on SEM images at low magnification of the whole cross-sectional area from a cube printed for chemical analysis (3 × 3 × 4 mm 3  after cutting from the baseplate). 5–15 images ( n ) were taken from the surface and each of the two sides, depending on the magnification, which is necessary to cover the full length of the respective side. The area of the oxide,  A Ti-oxide , on the respective surface and its length,  l Surface ,  is determined for each SEM image, and  δ ox  is calculated by: 1 \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
